Package: hotShiny
Type: Package
Title: Shiny-Compatible Reactive Framework with Hot Reloading
Version: 0.3.0
Authors@R: person("Jesus", "Rodriguez", role = c("aut", "cre"),
    email = "jrodriguezperez@darkpeakanalytics.com")
Description: A drop-in replacement for 'shiny' that runs apps on its own
    reactive engine, which records the reactive graph of every session so it
    can be inspected, diffed and hot-reloaded while preserving state. The UI
    layer, client (shiny.js) and wire protocol are Shiny's own, so apps,
    extension packages and htmlwidgets render and behave as they do under
    'shiny'. Apps written with 'hotShiny' can be published to plain 'shiny'
    with publish_to_shiny().
License: MIT + file LICENSE
Encoding: UTF-8
